KNOWNBUG
member_assignment3.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.s\.lo == 4'b0101: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(##1 main\.s == 165\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The transition relation composes the next-state value of s from the
slice for s.hi and, for the unassigned slice of s.lo, bits extracted
from the struct-typed symbol s. The bit-level layout of a packed struct
has the first member as the most significant, but the extraction is
applied to the struct directly rather than to its bit-vector
representation, and hence yields the bits of the wrong member.
